    abstract connected: bool with get, set
    /// <summary>
    /// The <c>process.allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags</c> property is a special,
    /// read-only <c>Set</c> of flags allowable within the <c>NODE_OPTIONS</c> environment variable.
    /// <br /><br />
    /// <c>process.allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags</c> extends <c>Set</c>, but overrides <c>Set.prototype.has</c> to recognize several different possible flag
    /// representations. <c>process.allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags.has()</c> will
    /// return <c>true</c> in the following cases:
    /// <br /><br />
    /// * Flags may omit leading single (<c>-</c>) or double (<c>--</c>) dashes; e.g., <c>inspect-brk</c> for <c>--inspect-brk</c>, or <c>r</c> for <c>-r</c>.
    /// * Flags passed through to V8 (as listed in <c>--v8-options</c>) may replace
    /// one or more _non-leading_ dashes for an underscore, or vice-versa;
    /// e.g., <c>--perf_basic_prof</c>, <c>--perf-basic-prof</c>, <c>--perf_basic-prof</c>,
    /// etc.
    /// * Flags may contain one or more equals (<c>=</c>) characters; all
    /// characters after and including the first equals will be ignored;
    /// e.g., <c>--stack-trace-limit=100</c>.
    /// * Flags _must_ be allowable within <c>NODE_OPTIONS</c>.
    /// <br /><br />
    /// When iterating over <c>process.allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags</c>, flags will
    /// appear only _once_; each will begin with one or more dashes. Flags
    /// passed through to V8 will contain underscores instead of non-leading
    /// dashes:
    /// <code lang="js">
    /// import { allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags } from 'node:process';
    ///
    /// allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags.forEach((flag) =&gt; {
    ///   // -r
    ///   // --inspect-brk
    ///   // --abort_on_uncaught_exception
    ///   // ...
    /// });
    /// </code>
    /// <br /><br />
    /// The methods <c>add()</c>, <c>clear()</c>, and <c>delete()</c> of<c>process.allowedNodeEnvironmentFlags</c> do nothing, and will fail
    /// silently.
    /// <br /><br />
