    /// If the value is an array, this is equivalent to calling this method multiple
    /// times.
    /// <br /><br />
    /// If there were no previous values for the header, this is equivalent to calling <c>outgoingMessage.setHeader(name, value)</c>.
    /// <br /><br />
    /// Depending of the value of <c>options.uniqueHeaders</c> when the client request or the
    /// server were created, this will end up in the header being sent multiple times or
    /// a single time with values joined using <c>; </c>.
